%U A400138 4,8,2,12,2,4,6,6,4,8,2,8,4,4,2,12,4,4,4,8,2,12,4
%N A400138 The number of divisors d of n such that gcid(d, n/d) is squarefree, where gcid is the greatest common infinitary divisor.
%C A400138 First differs from A365680, A366991, A399828, and A399831 at n = 32.
%C A400138 First differs from A252505, A365173, and A400141 at n = 64.
%C A400138 First differs from A390555 at n = 128.
%H A400138 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A400138/b400138.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A400138 Multiplicative with a(p^e) = A114212(e).
%t A400138 f[p_, e_] := 2^DigitSum[e, 2] + 2^DigitSum[Floor[(e-2)/2], 2] * (1 - Mod[e, 2]);
%t A400138 a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 100]
%o A400138 (PARI) f(e) = 2^hammingweight(e) + 2^hammingweight((e-2)\2) * (1-e%2);
%o A400138 a(n) = vecprod(apply(f, factor(n)[, 2]));
%Y A400138 Cf. A005117, A252505 (gcd), A114212, A399828 (gcud), A400137.
%Y A400138 Cf. A252505, A365173, A365680, A366991, A390555, A399831.
%Y A400138 The number of divisors d of n such that gcid(d, n/d) is: A037445 (1), this sequence (squarefree), A400139 (powerful), A400140 (square), A400141 (exponentially odd), A400142 (odd), A400143 (power of 2).
